    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_list" kindref="compound">ImmutableList</ref> - This class represents an immutable (functional) list. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It is implemented as a smart pointer (wraps <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_list_impl" kindref="compound">ImmutableListImpl</ref>), so it it is intended to always be copied by value as if it were a pointer. This interface matches <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_set" kindref="compound">ImmutableSet</ref> and <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_map" kindref="compound">ImmutableMap</ref>. <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_list" kindref="compound">ImmutableList</ref> objects should almost never be created directly, and instead should be created by <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_immutable_list_factory" kindref="compound">ImmutableListFactory</ref> objects that manage the lifetime of a group of lists. When the factory object is reclaimed, all lists created by that factory are released as well. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
